3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(180 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(207.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p90c46ee583\"><rect x=\"30.4\" y=\"10.472\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · What Greenleaf is worth to Tidewell ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Standalone: $8M × 10 = <b>$80M</b>.</p> <p>Cost synergies: $2M × 10 = $20M. Revenue synergies: $15M × 25% = $3.75M a year; at a 50% chance, $1.875M × 10 = $18.8M. Integration: −$6M.</p> <p>Value to Tidewell: <b>$112.8M</b>, just above the $110M asking price.</p>"},{"q":"So should Tidewell pay $110M?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>At $110M Tidewell keeps only $2.8M of the value it creates, and that depends on the uncertain sales synergies. If they don't happen, the deal is worth $94M: <b>Tidewell overpays by $16M</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> buy, but pay up front only for what Tidewell controls (about $94M), and pay for the sales upside only if it arrives.</p>"},{"q":"How would you structure the offer?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Up front: about $94M</b>, the standalone value plus cost savings less integration ($80M + $20M − $6M); open lower, around $88M, to leave room to negotiate</li> <li><b>Earn-out:</b> up to $16M more over three years if Greenleaf's sales through Tidewell's stores reach agreed targets. The sellers reach their $110M only if the sales synergy arrives</li> <li><b>Keep the founders</b> for two years, with part of the earn-out tied to their staying; the brand's appeal is in its founder story</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Buy Greenleaf, but not for $110M up front. On its own it is worth about $80M; certain cost savings add $20M and integration costs $6M, so Tidewell should pay about $94M up front. The extra-sales synergy is worth about $19M but is a coin flip, so pay for it through an earn-out tied to sales targets. Total value to Tidewell is about $113M, so offering $110M up front would hand almost all of it to the sellers. Risk: losing the founders, so tie part of the earn-out to their staying.","great":["Values the target on its own first","Separates certain cost synergies from uncertain revenue synergies","Sets a walk-away price","Uses deal structure (earn-out) to share risk"],"id":63,"slug":"tidewell-foods"}